# Random modules as layouts-1.test's, with --arrays: a quarter of the types
# of one constructor of two to four fields, flat records when their fields
# are flat, and each type's values in arrays, which hold records inline,
# set and read in monomorphic and polymorphic code, copied, resized,
# filled, written, unified and compared (see
# utils/codegen-oracle/generate-layout-programs.py): merkc's programs, at -O0
# and -O2, and with heap chunks of 64 bytes, print what mmc's print. The seed
# is fixed, so the modules are too; to search further, run
# generate-layout-programs.py --arrays with other seeds.
#
# REQUIRES: mmc
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir %t
# RUN: %python %S/../../../utils/codegen-oracle/generate-layout-programs.py --seed 1 --count 20 --arrays %t
# RUN: %compare-runs --levels 0 2 --chunk-bytes 64 --jobs 4 %t/*.m
